{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int INF = 1000*1000*1000;\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to, rev, cap, cost;\n};\n\nvoid add_edge(vector<vector<Edge>>& g, int from, int to, int cap, int cost) {\n    g[from].push_back({to, (int)g[to].size(), cap, cost});\n    g[to].push_back({from, (int)g[from].size()-1, 0, -cost});\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int N, m, k, c, d;\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d\", &N, &m, &k, &c, &d);\n    int n = N * 101 + 2;\n    vector<vector<Edge>> g(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        int x;\n        scanf(\"%d\", &x);\n        x--;\n        add_edge(g, n-2, x*101, 1, 0);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < 101; i++) {\n        add_edge(g, i, n-1, INF, i*c);\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j+1 < 101; j++) {\n            add_edge(g, i*101 + j, i*101 + j + 1, INF, 0);\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n        int u, v;\n        scanf(\"%d %d\", &u, &v);\n        u--; v--;\n        for (int j = 0; j+1 < 101; j++) {\n            for (int K = 1; K <= k; K++) {\n                int cost = d * (2*K - 1);\n                add_edge(g, u*101 + j, v*101 + j + 1, 1, cost);\n                add_edge(g, v*101 + j, u*101 + j + 1, 1, cost);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    int s = n-2, t = n-1;\n    int flow = 0, cost = 0;\n    while (flow < k) {\n        vector<int> dist(n, INF);\n        vector<int> prev(n, -1);\n        vector<int> preve(n, -1);\n        dist[s] = 0;\n        // Bellman-Ford (V-1 iterations)\n        for (int iter = 0; iter < n-1; iter++) {\n            bool updated = false;\n            for (int v = 0; v < n; v++) {\n                if (dist[v] == INF) continue;\n                for (int i = 0; i < (int)g[v].size(); i++) {\n                    Edge& e = g[v][i];\n                    if (e.cap > 0 && dist[v] + e.cost < dist[e.to]) {\n                        dist[e.to] = dist[v] + e.cost;\n                        prev[e.to] = v;\n                        preve[e.to] = i;\n                        updated = true;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (!updated) break;\n        }\n        if (dist[t] == INF) break;\n        int addflow = k - flow;\n        for (int v = t; v != s; v = prev[v]) {\n            addflow = min(addflow, g[prev[v]][preve[v]].cap);\n        }\n        for (int v = t; v != s; v = prev[v]) {\n            Edge& e = g[prev[v]][preve[v]];\n            e.cap -= addflow;\n            g[v][e.rev].cap += addflow;\n            cost += e.cost * addflow;\n        }\n        flow += addflow;\n    }\n    assert(flow == k);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", cost);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int INF = 1000 * 1000 * 1000;\n\n    static class Edge {\n        int to, rev, cap, cost;\n\n        Edge(int to, int rev, int cap, int cost) {\n            this.to = to;\n            this.rev = rev;\n            this.cap 